  "threeJsNotes": [
    "Load with GLTFLoader; WebP textures need no extra loader (EXT_texture_webp). No Draco/meshopt compression is applied; run gltf-transform (dedup, meshopt, resize) in the build if you want a smaller download.",
    "Convert repeated vegetation to InstancedMesh per variant at load: group meshes by geometry.uuid under GrassPatches, PlacedRocks, FlowerClusters, PlacedPlants (~2,600 nodes collapse to ~20 draw calls). Keep tree and bush leaf clusters as individual meshes, or instance per cluster mesh, if you need per-cluster sway.",
    "The environment GLB renders ~1.19M triangles, of which ~770k are grass. For mobile, drop Grass_Clump_C/D instances beyond ~25 m from the camera or halve the grass instance count.",
    "Set material.alphaTest = 0.5 on M_Foliage if the loader leaves it at default; avoid transparent: true on foliage.",
    "Grass is placed only inside the camera's view wedge from GardenEntrance (about +/-45 degrees); the clearing's back and sides rely on the terrain albedo. Re-run garden_assemble.py with a wider wedge if the camera path changes.",
    "Asset GLB: the variant root nodes are laid out in rows for inspection (group empties offset at x = 200 in Blender). Reset root.position to (0,0,0) before instancing.",
    "No lights, cameras, water or sky are exported. Recommended look: warm sun from camera-right/behind (~35 degrees elevation), blue gradient sky, light distance fog to soften the far terrain edge."
  ]
